--- Key Findings ---
1. SPECK-64 is the fastest lightweight cipher in SOFTWARE (ARX friendly to CPU/GPU pipelines)
2. PRESENT-80 is the smallest in HARDWARE (bit permutation + small S-box = tiny gate count)
3. AES-128 without hardware support (AES-NI) is ~21x slower than SPECK and ~4x faster than PRESENT
4. GPU acceleration benefits SPECK more than PRESENT (~49x vs ~508x over CPU) because:
   - SPECK's ARX ops are register-only → no memory latency, no S-box table lookups
   - PRESENT's bit-permutation benefits less from SIMT parallelism
5. CBC mode is always slower than CTR (sequential dependency in CBC encrypt)
6. CTR mode is the natural choice for GPU (embarrassingly parallel keystream generation)

